---
description: "Data integrity and integration safety. Apply for API, DB, server, prisma, and data-layer edits."
globs:
  - "**/api/**/*"
  - "**/server/**/*"
  - "**/prisma/**/*"
  - "**/*schema*.*"
  - "**/db/**/*"
  - "**/lib/**/*.{ts,js}"
alwaysApply: false
---

# Data Integrity & Integrations

- No delete/wipe/schema/bulk mutate without explicit approval; prefer migrations with rollback.
- Validate all untrusted input (users, uploads, webhooks, upstream APIs).
- Never embed secrets in code, docs, logs, or client bundles.
- Before changing APIs/DB/auth/FS/vendors: map callers; handle timeout, empty, duplicate, auth expiry, partial failure; fail closed.
- Do not delete “unused” code without search/tests; report rationale and rollback.
- Manage temp/logs/cache/build artifacts via `.gitignore` and ops policy.

Korean rationale: `docs/pvc-guide/ko/architecture/data-integrity.md`
